<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gryphon, Gryphon (album)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1973</span><span class="sg-chain-h">folk-rock arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Mainstream (Peter Howell, BBC Radiophonic Workshop)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1983</span><span class="sg-chain-h">electronic arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Swingle Singers, 1812 (album)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1989</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">King Henry's Madrigal (Jethro Tull)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Past Time with Good Company (Blackmore's Night, Under a Violet Moon)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">folk-rock version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Legacy of Tudors (Serenity)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2013</span><span class="sg-chain-h">first verse used as the opening</span></li></ul></section>
